   "subject": "Re: predictable color assignment",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Giovanni,\r<br>\r<br>You can use scale_colour_manual.\r<br>\r<br>Hadley\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On Sat, Aug 25, 2012 at 6:49 AM, Giovanni Azua &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">brav...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hello,\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I plot runtime to compare different implementations (or kernels) in the\r<br>&gt; following way. How can I make sure that my kernels labeled kernel1, kernel2,\r<br>&gt; kernel3 predictably get a consistent color assignment e.g. I would like\r<br>&gt; kernel1 to be the red etc.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; p &lt;- ggplot(data=df, aes(x=n, y=rt, group=kernel, shape=kernel,\r<br>&gt; colour=kernel)) + geom_point(fill=&quot;white&quot;, size=3) + geom_line() + xlab(&quot;n&quot;)\r<br>&gt; + ylab(&quot;Runtime (s)&quot;) +\r<br>&gt; opts(title=title,plot.title=theme_text(size=font.size))\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"http://dev.new\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://dev.new&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374853955000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0nD8KdC6JJ7RPX7MajpsbH\">dev.new</a>(width=7, height=5)\r<br>&gt; p\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Many TIA,\r<br>&gt; Best!\r<br>&gt; Giovanni\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "&gt; --\r<br>&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing\r<br>&gt; list.\r<br>&gt; Please provide a reproducible example:\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374853955000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3mVeDc8S_9RlaKMbnJCQyn\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a>\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; To post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a>\r<br>&gt; To unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a>\r<br>&gt; More options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374853955000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3l-ePKNONQ9ME7HdBwuOXa\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a>\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>-- \r<br>Assistant Professor\r<br>Department of Statistics / Rice University\r<br><a href=\"http://had.co.nz/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://had.co.nz/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374853955000&amp;usg=AOvVaw34BkZzxIqzYfQYEDdJdQk-\">http://had.co.nz/</a>\r<br>"
